          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(pin (num \"48\") (name \"VCAP\") (type \"power_out\"))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The UART3 interface cannot work as intended, and external loading or signaling on the connector may disrupt or damage the MCU's internal core supply.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["FCC1", "NAVC1", "HSE1", "HSE2", "C14", "C30", "C37", "C38"],
      "pins": ["FCC1.5", "FCC1.37", "FCC1.12", "FCC1.13", "NAVC1.5", "NAVC1.6"],
      "nets": ["HSE_IN_FCC", "HSE_OUT_FCC", "HSE_IN_NAVC", "HSE_OUT_NAVC", "Net-(FCC1-PH0)", "VREF+_FCC", "Net-(NAVC1-PH0)", "Net-(NAVC1-PH1)"],
      "observed": "FCC HSE nets connect to pins PE6 and PE7 rather than its PH0/PH1 oscillator pins. NAVC HSE nets do not connect to NAVC1; its PH0/PH1 pins instead connect to C37/C38.",
      "expected": "The 25 MHz external crystals should connect to the HSE oscillator pins of their respective MCUs. The specification identifies an HSE crystal for both MCUs.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"HSE_IN_FCC\") ... (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"PE6\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"HSE_OUT_FCC\") ... (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"37\") (pinfunction \"PE7\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"HSE_IN_NAVC\") ... (ref \"HSE2\") (pin \"1\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"HSE_OUT_NAVC\") ... (ref \"R32\") (pin \"1\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "HSE crystal (both MCUs) | ABM8G-25.000MHZ-4Y-T3"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The MCU high-speed external clocks will not operate as intended, preventing or compromising normal MCU startup and clocking.",
      "confidence": 0.98
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist shows critical departures from the intended board: both MCUs have unpowered supply pins, the FCC UART3 connector is wired to VCAP pins, and the external crystal nets are misconnected or detached from the MCU oscillator pins. These faults would prevent the board from behaving as specified."
}

